  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Chez Mô is a large seafood brasserie set right by the sea, between the ramparts of Antibes' old town and Cap d'Antibes. Fishmonger counter, sushi bar, seafood platters and water views: it's a generous, unpretentious address, designed for a meal with your feet almost in the water.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>A blog specialising in dog-friendly outings in Antibes lists Chez Mô among the addresses that accept animals. This information comes from a third-party blog and not from the restaurant's official website (chezmo-antibes.fr), which does not detail a dog policy as of this fiche's writing: a phone call before you come lets you confirm, especially on the terrace during peak season. Service is continuous, 7 days a week, from 12pm to 10pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the terrace sits right on the coastal road — keep your dog on a short leash when arriving and leaving, traffic can be heavy in summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Cap d'Antibes coastal trail starts not far from here, a good option for a walk with your dog after the meal, between coves and umbrella pines.</p>
    </div>

